WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.187 --> 00:00:15.292
At last Miles and Edward had their day in court.

2
00:00:16.353 --> 00:00:18.394
The judge asked them to state their full names.

3
00:00:18.414 --> 00:00:20.895
"King Edward."

4
00:00:22.917 --> 00:00:24.017
The judge looked at Edward.

5
00:00:24.037 --> 00:00:28.540
"Would you like to try again, young man?"

6
00:00:30.940 --> 00:00:31.921
Edward shook his head.

7
00:00:31.941 --> 00:00:33.741
"Not really."

8
00:00:37.964 --> 00:00:39.865
The judge sighed and moved on to Miles.

9
00:00:39.885 --> 00:00:42.526
"And you?

10
00:00:43.646 --> 00:00:46.848
I suppose you're another member of the royal family?"

11
00:00:46.868 --> 00:00:50.250
"No, I'm Miles Hendon."

12
00:00:53.671 --> 00:00:54.732
The judge sighed again.

13
00:00:56.212 --> 00:01:02.498
"You do know that you're on trial for claiming to be Miles Hendon and the rightful owner of

14
00:01:02.538 --> 00:01:03.499
Hendon Hall?

15
00:01:04.980 --> 00:01:08.123
As well as for pushing Hugh Hendon?"

16
00:01:10.926 --> 00:01:12.847
Now it was Miles' turn to sigh.

17
00:01:12.867 --> 00:01:21.235
"Yes." During the trial Hugh described Miles as a "dangerous beggar," and Miles had to be restrained from

18
00:01:21.315 --> 00:01:22.136
pushing him again.

19
00:01:23.968 --> 00:01:27.251
The judge sentenced Miles to sit for two hours in the stocks.

20
00:01:30.834 --> 00:01:38.100
"As for you," the judge said to Edward, "I'm tempted to give you the same punishment for being

21
00:01:38.140 --> 00:01:39.521
in such bad company.

22
00:01:40.782 --> 00:01:44.465
You should know better than to associate with such a rough criminal."

23
00:01:44.485 --> 00:01:48.188
"He's not a rough criminal!

24
00:01:49.249 --> 00:01:52.272
He's my friend and a knight—" "Enough!"

25
00:01:52.932 --> 00:01:54.273
Miles silenced Edward.

26
00:01:54.293 --> 00:01:59.795
"As I was saying," the judge said to Edward.

27
00:01:59.815 --> 00:02:02.816
"I hope you've learned your lesson.

28
00:02:03.996 --> 00:02:08.198
If I find you making trouble again, you'll go straight to the stocks."

29
00:02:10.518 --> 00:02:14.840
Edward muttered under his breath while Miles sent him frantic signals to be quiet.

30
00:02:18.512 --> 00:02:22.855
Miles was led to the stocks in the village square with Edward following along for support.

31
00:02:24.176 --> 00:02:27.799
As soon as Miles sat down, people began to mock and insult him.

32
00:02:29.700 --> 00:02:33.362
When someone hurled an egg at Miles, that was too much for Edward.

33
00:02:33.382 --> 00:02:35.684
"Shame on all of you!"

34
00:02:36.184 --> 00:02:36.885
Edward cried.

35
00:02:36.905 --> 00:02:40.647
"This is my servant and a knight in my court.

36
00:02:41.688 --> 00:02:42.609
Set him free.

37
00:02:43.069 --> 00:02:45.651
I am—" "Edward, stop!"

38
00:02:46.131 --> 00:02:46.912
Miles shouted.

39
00:02:47.916 --> 00:02:49.698
"You'll only get yourself in trouble."

40
00:02:50.999 --> 00:02:53.741
Then he called to the sheriff, who was staring at Edward.

41
00:02:53.761 --> 00:02:56.022
"Pay no attention to the lad.

42
00:02:56.243 --> 00:02:56.783
He's ill."

43
00:02:58.745 --> 00:03:00.146
The sheriff approached Edward.

44
00:03:00.166 --> 00:03:03.268
"You need to mind your manners.

45
00:03:04.489 --> 00:03:07.351
A couple hours in the stocks might straighten you out."

46
00:03:07.371 --> 00:03:13.056
"Let's make it six," said Hugh, who had arrived to watch Miles suffer.

47
00:03:14.792 --> 00:03:18.375
The sheriff grabbed Edward and started to drag him over to the stocks.

48
00:03:19.535 --> 00:03:22.257
Edward was so shocked that he couldn't even protest.

49
00:03:23.538 --> 00:03:24.278
"Let him go!"

50
00:03:24.758 --> 00:03:25.579
Miles shouted.

51
00:03:25.599 --> 00:03:28.360
"I'll sit here for six more hours in his place."

52
00:03:28.380 --> 00:03:31.662
"No!" Edward screamed.

53
00:03:31.682 --> 00:03:36.305
"Don't—" "I'm warning you, lad," Hugh said.

54
00:03:36.325 --> 00:03:40.908
"For every word you utter, your friend will spend another hour in the stocks."

55
00:03:43.120 --> 00:03:47.503
Because of his own punishment and Edward's, Miles spent much of the day in the stocks.

56
00:03:49.244 --> 00:03:52.006
At one point Edward approached him with a small branch.

57
00:03:53.367 --> 00:03:55.789
The young king touched him lightly on each shoulder.

58
00:03:55.809 --> 00:04:00.132
"You are now an earl," Edward said to his friend.

59
00:04:01.412 --> 00:04:03.554
Miles couldn't help but smile at this honor.

60
00:04:05.395 --> 00:04:09.678
And his hours in the stocks gave him plenty of time to think about what to do next.

61
00:04:09.698 --> 00:04:12.360
"Should we return to the city?"

62
00:04:12.864 --> 00:04:13.465
he wondered.

63
00:04:13.485 --> 00:04:18.048
"I'm going to need someone powerful to help me before I challenge Hugh again.

64
00:04:19.289 --> 00:04:21.531
But where can I find someone like that?"

65
00:04:24.693 --> 00:04:27.755
After about four hours, Miles thought of a possibility.

66
00:04:27.775 --> 00:04:31.238
"Blake said the new king was kind and merciful.

67
00:04:32.519 --> 00:04:36.602
Maybe I could talk to him, but would he believe the word of a penniless stranger?"

68
00:04:38.023 --> 00:04:39.144
Miles thought some more.

69
00:04:40.512 --> 00:04:42.893
"My father had a friend at court, Sir Marlow.

70
00:04:44.173 --> 00:04:47.214
He was in charge of King Henry's kitchen or stables or something.

71
00:04:48.774 --> 00:04:49.795
Maybe he could help me.

72
00:04:50.895 --> 00:04:51.995
Yes, that's it!

73
00:04:52.576 --> 00:04:55.016
We'll go to the palace, and I'll ask Sir Marlow for help."

74
00:04:57.637 --> 00:05:00.958
When Miles was finally released, he was ordered to leave the village.

75
00:05:02.679 --> 00:05:07.020
He wanted to go to the palace but had second thoughts about taking Edward back to the city.

76
00:05:08.076 --> 00:05:12.900
"Edward keeps insisting on going to the coronation," Miles thought as they left the square.

77
00:05:12.920 --> 00:05:16.723
"Who knows how the excitement will affect his illness?

78
00:05:17.824 --> 00:05:19.706
What will happen when he's not crowned?"

79
00:05:20.907 --> 00:05:24.770
But there was no discouraging Edward, who'd been busy planning his return.

80
00:05:24.790 --> 00:05:31.956
"By my calculations," he said happily, "we should arrive on the night before the coronation."

81
00:05:34.518 --> 00:05:36.500
And that's exactly what happened.

82
00:05:37.584 --> 00:05:41.386
Miles and Edward arrived at night to find the city already celebrating.

83
00:05:42.967 --> 00:05:45.708
But Edward hadn't anticipated what would happen next.

84
00:05:46.988 --> 00:05:50.910
As they approached the bridge, Miles and Edward lost each other in the crowd.

85
00:05:53.832 --> 00:05:57.593
Edward made his way to the cathedral where the coronation would take place.

86
00:05:58.954 --> 00:06:03.236
Dressed in rags, hungry and tired, the real king stood near the door.

87
00:06:05.620 --> 00:06:10.747
Watching workers streaming into and out of the cathedral, he waited for just the right moment.

88
00:06:12.850 --> 00:06:17.455
Then Edward slipped into the cathedral behind a carpenter and found a hiding place.
